- Source: TypeSafe AI (`jev-1.13` — verified model identity, zero verified public benchmarks)
- Date: 2026-10-01 (UTC)
- Overview and scoring methodology: `../../model-comparison.md`
- Cross-model signed log: `../../model-findings.md`

## Verified identity (no benchmarks)

- **What it is:** Jev 1.13 is a **System One model from TypeSafe AI** for fast,
  structured decisions — verified via OpenCode Zen docs
  (https://opencode.ai/docs/zen, "Jev" section) and TypeSafe AI docs
  (https://docs.typesafe.ai/). Instead of generating text, it evaluates a
  `state` against typed questions and returns values and probabilities the
  calling code consumes directly (no text generation, no parsing).
- **API contract:** OpenCode Zen `opencode/jev-1.13` at
  `https://opencode.ai/zen/v1/systemone` (not Chat Completions / Responses).
  Three question types: yes/no (`noul`, 0–1), multiple-choice (`choice` with
  probabilities + confidence), rubric-based (`score` with probabilities +
  confidence). Questions evaluate in parallel and in isolation against the
  same state; adding questions barely changes response time (no context-rot).
- **Free variant:** `jev-1.13-free` — limited-time free model on Zen
  (Free/Free per-token; standard tier $0.042 input / Free output per 1M).
- **Training:** RLCD — reinforcement learning for calibrated decisions
  (TypeSafe AI AI primer); RLHF co-inventor Diogo Almeida is a TypeSafe
  cofounder. Prompts/inputs not used for training (Zen privacy section).
- **Not to be confused with:** AutoTrust AI Lab's `JEV-27B` / `JEV-27B-VL` /
  `JEV-9B` decision models (https://huggingface.co/autotrust) — a different
  vendor's model family; their benchmark results cannot be attributed to
  TypeSafe AI's Jev 1.13.

## Why no scored file

- Standard LLM benchmarks (GPQA Diamond, HLE, SWE-bench, LiveCodeBench,
  Terminal-Bench, MRCR/RULER, Artificial Analysis Intelligence Index): no
  verified public score found for Jev 1.13 — HF hosts no `JEV-1.13` model
  (HF search + AutoTrust org checked 2026-10-01), and TypeSafe AI's docs
  publish no eval numbers, only the API contract and calibration philosophy.
- As a System One decision API the model does not generate text, so the
  six-dimension text-model scorecard (Tool use / Reasoning / Context window /
  Multimodal / Coding / Cost efficiency) has no verified raw numbers to
  normalize. Zero verified benchmarks → self-exclusion per
  `model-report-TEMPLATE.md` SELF-EXCLUSION and `RULES.md`.
- Re-rate only if TypeSafe AI publishes verified eval numbers for Jev 1.13
  (or a peer rater supplies same-harness measurements).
